    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but when you look at the \"pro\" side, like for crime prevention and stuff, do people actually see it as a proven success? or is it more of a theoretical thing that's just being pushed because it's new tech? i'm trying to figure out if the security benefits are actually well-documented or if it's just hype.",
