    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that. but if it's mostly anecdotal, wouldn't it be pretty reckless to roll it out on such a massive scale in cities? like, if we don't even know for sure if it works, shouldn't we just halt the rollout until we have actual proof, rather than risking people's privacy for something that might just be hype?",
